[{"id":126193,"sender_id":51,"sender_full_name":"Ulrik","avatar_url":"https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/e499ead5270df65e0b599d630ce0f40b?d=identicon&version=1","content":"<p><a href=\"#narrow/channel/2-Latest-Changes/topic/Lazard.27s.20criterion/near/126193\">#5</a> Add a reference to Jonas Frey’s clan version</p>\n<p><a href=\"https://ncatlab.org/nlab/revision/diff/Lazard%27s+criterion/4\">diff</a>, <a href=\"https://ncatlab.org/nlab/revision/Lazard%27s+criterion/4\">v4</a>, <a href=\"https://ncatlab.org/nlab/show/Lazard%27s+criterion\">current</a></p>","timestamp":1791367278,"subject":"Lazard's criterion","stream_id":2,"display_recipient":"Latest Changes","reactions":[]},{"id":126194,"sender_id":11,"sender_full_name":"Urs","avatar_url":"https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/b00d1ee17463af676c78974439b92471?d=identicon&version=1","content":"<p><a href=\"#narrow/channel/2-Latest-Changes/topic/Lazard.27s.20criterion/near/126194\">#6</a> It looks to me like Frey 2026 only recalls the abstract part of Lazard’s criterion (and doesn’t claim to do more) which can be cited from EGA4 or Borceux (and that’s what Frey does). I have reworded to the following clarification:</p>\n<hr>\n<p>Regarding <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>R</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">R</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.6833em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0077em;\">R</span></span></span></span>-<a href=\"https://ncatlab.org/nlab/show/modules\">modules</a> as <a href=\"https://ncatlab.org/nlab/show/algebra%20over%20a%20Lawvere%20theory\">models</a> of the <a href=\"https://ncatlab.org/nlab/show/Lawvere%20theory\">Lawvere theory</a> of <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>R</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">R</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.6833em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0077em;\">R</span></span></span></span>-modules, whose <a href=\"https://ncatlab.org/nlab/show/representable%20functor\">representable</a> models are the finitely generated free ones, Lazard’s criterion (Prop. \\ref{LazardCriterion}) splits into two parts:</p>\n<ol>\n<li>The formal part is the general fact that a model is a <a href=\"https://ncatlab.org/nlab/show/filtered%20colimit\">filtered colimit</a> of <a href=\"https://ncatlab.org/nlab/show/representable%20functor\">representable models</a> iff its <a href=\"https://ncatlab.org/nlab/show/category%20of%20elements\">category of elements</a> is <a href=\"https://ncatlab.org/nlab/show/filtered%20category\">filtered</a>, i.e. iff it is <a href=\"https://ncatlab.org/nlab/show/flat%20functor\">flat as a functor</a> on the theory.</li>\n</ol>\n<p>(This is classical, cf. <a href=\"https://ncatlab.org/nlab/show/SGA4\">SGA4</a> Exp. I; <a href=\"https://ncatlab.org/nlab/show/Handbook%20of%20Categorical%20Algebra\">Borceux 1994</a> §I.6.3. For models of <a href=\"https://ncatlab.org/nlab/show/clans\">clans</a>, which include models of all algebraic theories via finite-product clans, this is stated as Frey 2026 Lem. 5.4, where it is likewise deduced from <a href=\"https://ncatlab.org/nlab/show/Handbook%20of%20Categorical%20Algebra\">Borceux 1994</a> §I.6.3.) </p>\n<ol>\n<li>The genuinely module-theoretic content of Lazard’s criterion is that this categorical flatness coincides with <a href=\"https://ncatlab.org/nlab/show/flat%20module\">flatness of the module</a> in the sense of <a href=\"https://ncatlab.org/nlab/show/homological%20algebra\">homological algebra</a>.</li>\n</ol>\n<hr>\n<p><a href=\"https://ncatlab.org/nlab/revision/diff/Lazard%27s+criterion/5\">diff</a>, <a href=\"https://ncatlab.org/nlab/revision/Lazard%27s+criterion/5\">v5</a>, <a href=\"https://ncatlab.org/nlab/show/Lazard%27s+criterion\">current</a></p>","timestamp":1791369501,"subject":"Lazard's criterion","stream_id":2,"display_recipient":"Latest Changes","reactions":[]},{"id":126195,"sender_id":51,"sender_full_name":"Ulrik","avatar_url":"https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/e499ead5270df65e0b599d630ce0f40b?d=identicon&version=1","content":"<p><a href=\"#narrow/channel/2-Latest-Changes/topic/Lazard.27s.20criterion/near/126195\">#7</a> Ah thanks for that clarification!</p>","timestamp":1791370181,"subject":"Lazard's criterion","stream_id":2,"display_recipient":"Latest Changes","reactions":[]}]